(Why can position outweigh relevance\054 and what helps\077) Tj
T*
(In an autoregressive language model\054 information flows forward\072 later positions can use earlier information\054 not the other way around\056) Tj
T*
(Early information can ripple through many later positions\056) Tj
T*
(The final input position directly feeds the next\055word prediction\056 Residual connections can preserve the final position\222s own information\073 attention to nearby words can also help the end\056) Tj
T*
(The middle can miss both advantages\056 This is explanatory intuition\054 not a universal rule\056) Tj
T*
(Input workaround) Tj
T*
(Rank passages\054 put strong evidence near an edge\054 and test whether position changes shift accuracy\056) Tj
T*
(Adjust attention during answering) Tj
T*
(Reduce the attention advantage caused by position\054 so relevant passages receive more attention\056 This changes attention during answering\054 without retraining\056 Hsieh et al\056\054 2024) Tj
