(How they estimate reliability scores) Tj
T*
(For each question\054 they search each source separately and have the LLM answer with only that source\222s passages\056) Tj
T*
(If those passages don\222t support the answer\054 that source abstains\056) Tj
T*
(That gives a table of answers or abstentions across sources\056) Tj
T*
(They start with equal voting weight for every source\054 group answers with the same meaning\054 then see how often each source agrees with the consensus\054 updating weights until they stabilize\056) Tj
T*
(Finally\054 for a new question\054 they consult sources in reliability order and combine answers by weighted voting\054 without retraining the LLM\056) Tj
T*
(Next\054 we\222ll look at their weighted\055vote example\054 then experiments\056) Tj
T*
ET

Q

