(How do they build the test\077) Tj
T*
(They construct nine simulated sources\072 nine separate document collections\056) Tj
T*
(For each question\054 each source independently has a 60\045 chance of containing passages about that question\056) Tj
T*
(Being about the question does not mean being correct\056 Among covered questions\054 a low\055reliability source uses the true answer 10\045 of the time\073 a high\055reliability source uses it 90\045 of the time\056) Tj
T*
(Illustrative question\072 When did Bridge X open\077 \223It opened in 1937\224 and \223It opened in 1940\224 both address the question\054 but they cannot both give the correct year\056) Tj
T*
(They increase the number of unreliable sources and compare reliability\055weighted answers with equal voting\056) Tj
T*
