(One document can supply different pieces of evidence) Tj
T*
(What\222s the difference between eavestroughs and rain gutters\077) Tj
T*
(Eavestroughs and gutters are essentially the same thing\054 with eavestroughs being a specific type of gutter that is installed at the edge of a roof \1331a\054 2a\054 3a\135\056 An eavestrough is a trough that is connected to the eaves of a building\054 which are the sections of the roof that hang over the wall\054 and it is used to direct rainwater away from the roof and towards a drainage system \1332b\054 3b\135\056) Tj
T*
(Numbers identify source documents\073 letters identify selected spans within them\056) Tj
T*
(The first sentence cites \1331a\054 2a\054 3a\135\073 the second cites \1332b\054 3b\135\056) Tj
T*
(In document 2\054 span a supports the claim that gutter and eavestrough are synonyms\056) Tj
T*
(Span b supports the definition of an eavestrough as a trough under the eaves\056) Tj
T*
(Different sentences can cite different spans from the same document\056) Tj
T*
(Document 2) Tj
